<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mekong Delta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> Delta is the region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> where the Mekong River divides into many channels before reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-china-sea">South China Sea</a>. In the early centuries CE it was the heart of Funan, whose port at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oc-eo">Oc Eo</a> has yielded Roman and Indian objects. Settled by Vietnamese from the seventeenth century, it is now the country's main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>-growing region but is threatened by rising sea levels.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mekong-delta.jpg" alt="Mekong Delta" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bùi Thụy Đào Nguyên · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C%E1%BA%A7u_Cao_L%C3%A3nh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Water Chenla, on the <b>Mekong Delta</b>, had the river's wealth but was more exposed; late in the century it faced war from Javanese pirates who took the delta and then Chenla itself, and it came to depend on the Shailendra dynasty of Java and Srivijaya.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chenla">Chenla · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Chinese histories place its foundation in the 1st century CE in the <b>Mekong Delta</b>, though archaeology shows settlement there from at least the 4th century BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/funan">Funan · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Through its commercial reach the empire linked the economies of the Mediterranean with Arabia, East Africa, India and, indirectly, China, and Roman coins have been found as far afield as southern India and the <b>Mekong Delta</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Private trade was abolished in 1978, a measure that fell heavily on the ethnic Chinese Hoa of Cho Lon, and farmers in the <b>Mekong Delta</b> were pressed into collectives.</blockquote><a href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Socialist Republic of Vietnam · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Communist guerrillas in the <b>Mekong Delta</b> beat off a South Vietnamese attack backed by American helicopters and advisers.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January in history</a></li></ul></section>
